---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { labSamples } from '../../data/labSamples';
---
<Base lang="en" title="Technical lab | Miguel Quevedo" description="Independent Rust, C, Assembly, C++, Swift and PHP samples with explicit verification status.">
  <main id="contenido" class="detail-main wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/en/">← Back to portfolio</a>
    <div class="detail-hero lab-hero"><div><p class="section-kicker">CODE SAMPLES</p><h1>Technical lab<span>.</span></h1><p class="detail-lede">Small projects that explain an engineering decision and show its implementation.</p></div><div class="detail-badge">SAMPLES<br /><strong>5 PROJECTS</strong></div></div>
    <p class="lab-intro">These samples are independent of Meson and contain none of its private source. Rust, C, Assembly, C++ and PHP have locally executed tests. Swift includes tests that still need a host with Swift.</p>
    <div class="lab-grid">
      <article><span>01 / RUST</span><h2>Local synchronization</h2><p>Vector clocks, concurrent changes and pending operations until acknowledgment. Five tests executed.</p><div class="tags"><span>Rust</span><span>Verified</span></div><a class="text-link" href="/en/samples/local-sync/">View sample ↗</a></article>
      {labSamples.map((sample, index) => (
        <article><span>{String(index + 2).padStart(2, '0')} / {sample.en.eyebrow}</span><h2>{sample.en.title}</h2><p>{sample.en.lead}</p><div class="tags">{sample.stack.map((skill) => <span>{skill}</span>)}<span>{sample.verified ? 'Verified' : 'Execution pending'}</span></div><a class="text-link" href={`/en/samples/${sample.slug}/`}>View sample ↗</a></article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="lab-note"><strong>What the samples show</strong><p>The Astro site and Meson projects already show JavaScript, Dart and Kotlin in context. These new examples focus on languages with less visible authored code. Plain PHP does not demonstrate Laravel, and every new sample needs your personal review before you use it as professional evidence.</p></div>
  </main>
</Base>
